  "finalText": "I've built the quote as an 8-second, 1080×1080 piece with off-white type on a dark background and one orange accent. I checked it in a contact sheet at several times and it plays as planned. I didn't run the critique pass.\n\nThe four moments:\n1. **\"Design is not\"** (0.2–2.2 s): the words fade up one at a time, then the phrase slides up and fades out.\n2. **\"just what it looks like.\"** (2.0–4.4 s): the letters rise one by one, and the phrase exits upward as the next one starts.\n3. **\"Design is\" + \"how it works.\"** (4.2 s onward): \"Design is\" is small and grey. \"how it works.\" is huge, extra-bold and orange, and its words pop in with a spring overshoot (0.22 s apart).\n4. **Attribution** (6.2 s onward): a short orange rule scales out, then \"— Steve Jobs\" fades up small beneath it. The final frame holds until 8 s.\n\n\"how it works.\" is wide, with only a few pixels of margin on each side at 150 px. If you want more breathing room, I can drop it to about 135 px.\n\nI can also make the phrase handovers overlap more, add a subtle background shift when the orange phrase lands, or save a calmer and a punchier version to compare."
